{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "source": "# Map library desk guide\n\nCirculating maps may be borrowed by registered members. The standard loan lasts fourteen days. The checkout desk closes at 17:45.\n\nThe renewal form is yellow. A map loan can be renewed once unless another reader has reserved the map. Renewal requests must arrive before the due date.\n\nReturned folders go into the shallow tray. The librarian checks each returned map for tears before clearing the loan. A condition check completes the map return process.\n\nFragile maps are stabilized before they can be handled safely. A conservator repairs torn margins with thin tissue. The repair paste dries overnight.\n\nThe storage drawer has a brass handle. Flat storage and acid-free sleeves slow further damage to delicate maps. Each sleeve carries a pencil inventory number.\n\nThe exhibition case has a light meter. Illumination must remain below fifty lux for colored historic sheets. Limiting light exposure protects vulnerable map pigments.\n",
  "source_name": "library.md",
